      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Last time, the water escaped as steam, and we just let it go. To keep it, we have to catch that vapour and cool it back into a liquid. That's called distillation, and it works well for salt water. But with two liquids, like ethanol and water, a simple setup does a poor job, and adding a tall column packed with glass beads does a much better one. So why does a fractionating column improve liquid separation?",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
