          "end": 27.71600000000007,
          "score": 0.372
        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So what if we do it again? Condense that vapour, and boil the new liquid. Now the vapour is about eighty percent ethanol. Do it again, and it's about eighty six, then about eighty nine. Each cycle of boiling and condensing enriches the vapour, which means it raises the share of the more volatile liquid, the one that evaporates more easily. Notice the steps are getting smaller. Simple distillation gives you only one cycle. To separate two liquids well, you need many.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
    {
