      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "The beads matter because they give the vapour a huge surface to condense on, so lots of these little cycles happen in a short height. A longer column gives even more cycles, so the separation gets better. You collect the distillate in parts, called fractions. While the thermometer stays near seventy eight, the fraction is mostly ethanol. When the reading climbs towards a hundred, the ethanol is running out, so you swap in a new receiver.",
