      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So which should you choose? If one part doesn't evaporate at all, like salt in water, or the boiling points are far apart, one cycle is enough. That's simple distillation. If two liquids mix and their boiling points are close, use fractional distillation. You'll sometimes hear twenty five degrees apart as a rough guide, but it isn't a law. What matters is how much more easily one liquid evaporates, and how pure you need it. Oil refineries use giant columns like this to split crude oil into fractions, like petrol and diesel.",
