      "pronunciationText": "Ethanol catches fire easily, so it's heated with an electric heating mantle or a water bath, never a flame, with the apparatus clamped and the receiver open. Here's a way to remember the column. Simple distillation is one step up the ladder. A column climbs many steps, and the ladder ends at the azeotrope.",
