      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Use simple distillation. Heat the solution, and the water evaporates while the non-volatile dye stays in the flask. The vapour condenses in the condenser and collects as pure water. Filtration can't work, because the dye is dissolved. Its particles are far smaller than the pores, so they pass straight through with the water. Filtering out the dye is the slip to avoid.",
